{"id":"r6","level":1,"levelName":"Reading","n":6,"of":8,"title":"Vowels: a and e","titleHe":"נִקּוּד: a וְ־e","goal":"Read the four marks that make the a and e sounds.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Vowels are marks written under (mostly) the consonant they follow. So בַ is read ba, not ab — consonant first, then its vowel. Modern Hebrew has fewer vowel sounds than it has marks, so several marks share a sound."},{"type":"vowels","ids":["ַ","ָ","ֵ","ֶ"],"items":[{"sign":"ַ","on":"בַ","name":"פַּתַח","en":"patach","sound":"a as in father"},{"sign":"ָ","on":"בָ","name":"קָמַץ","en":"kamatz","sound":"a as in father"},{"sign":"ֵ","on":"בֵ","name":"צֵירֵי","en":"tsere","sound":"e as in they"},{"sign":"ֶ","on":"בֶ","name":"סֶגוֹל","en":"segol","sound":"e as in bed"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"פַּתַח and קָמַץ both say a. צֵירֵי and סֶגוֹל both say e. They look different and are spelled differently, but you pronounce each pair the same."}],"vocab":[{"he":"דָּג","en":"fish","translit":"dag"},{"he":"יָם","en":"sea","translit":"yam"},{"he":"אֵם","en":"mother","translit":"em"},{"he":"בֵּן","en":"son","translit":"ben"},{"he":"דֶּלֶת","en":"door","translit":"delet"},{"he":"עֶרֶב","en":"evening","translit":"erev"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["e as in they","e as in bed","i as in machine","a as in father"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בַ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["a as in father","i as in machine","e as in they","e as in bed"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בָ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["a as in father","e as in bed","a as in father","e as in they"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בֵ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["a as in father","e as in they","e as in bed","a as in father"],"correct":2,"prompt":"בֶ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["wakes up","fish","ring","to learn"],"correct":1,"prompt":"דָּג","translit":"dag"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["there","sea","development","strength, power"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יָם","translit":"yam"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["heavy","in, at","summer","mother"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אֵם","translit":"em"},{"type":"choice","q":"Which mark is kamatz?","options":["בֵ","בָ","בַ","בֶ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “mother”?","options":["רֶבַע","אֵם","קוֹרֵא","כָּאן"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["אֵם","יָם","עֶרֶב","בֵּן"],"correct":0,"say":"אֵם","he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["דָּג","fish"],["יָם","sea"],["אֵם","mother"],["בֵּן","son"],["דֶּלֶת","door"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"Which mark is patach?","options":["בָ","בֵ","בַ","בֶ"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “sea”?","options":["יָם","לִפְנֵי","שׁוֹאֵל","יוֹנָה"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"דָּג","translit":"dag","en":"fish"},{"type":"read","he":"בֵּן","translit":"ben","en":"son"},{"type":"type","q":"Write “door” in Hebrew","answer":"דֶּלֶת","hint":"delet"}]}